The attached image presents flow cytometry histograms demonstrating the effect of Nano-11 nanoparticles on the expression of costimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on dendritic cells (DCs). Incubation with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) for two days resulted in a marked increase in the expression of CD80 and CD86, as indicated by the significant rightward shift compared to the medium control (gray line). CD40 expression showed a less pronounced increase. These findings support Nano-11's role as a vaccine adjuvant by showing its ability to activate DCs in vitro, a critical step for initiating an effective immune response.